  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Exhibition Catalogue",
    "overview": "The Catalog is hung like a small exhibition: a Prussian-ink wall frames each page, and the reading happens on pale label stock below it. Each Game is a numbered plate with a wall label beside its cover, and the Score Breakdown is the catalogue's scholarly apparatus, ruled like a ledger so a reader can check the sum. The site's one job is to make a single number trustworthy, so the system spends its expression on the plate numeral, the Score numeral and the pull toward 70, and stays plain everywhere else.\n\nDensity is low and deliberate: one plate per row, generous vertical rhythm (2rem between plate rules), hairline dividers instead of boxes. Two faces split the work cleanly: Archivo, wide and heavy, is the wall vinyl (wordmark, plate numbers, headings, Score numerals, every control and label); Source Serif 4 is the printed label text and prose. In dark mode the whole page hangs on the wall: the reading ground becomes a deep Prussian, not a neutral grey.\n\nThe admin (`/admin`) is an Operate surface in the same world: same tokens and masthead colour, but Archivo carries all of its text and the expressive scale is turned down to a compact h1 and ruled sections.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Prussian-ink wall plus label-stock reading ground; every non-Score hue sits in the wall's blue family (hue 244–256).",
      "A five-step Score scale from clay to deep green, always printed as a number beside its colour.",
      "Archivo with its width axis (112–125%) for anything that names or counts; Source Serif 4 for anything that is read.",
      "Hairline rules, tabular figures, no nested containers.",
      "Unscored is shown as absence (a dash and a dashed empty scale), never as zero."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Wall Rule",
        "body": "Outside the Score scale and the admin states, every colour is a lightness or chroma step of the wall's blue (hue 244–256). A new surface adds no new hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Printed Number Rule",
        "body": "Colour is never the only signal. Every Score colour sits beside the printed numeral; every message state prints its word (\"Done\", \"Problem\", \"Check\") before the text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Absence Rule",
        "body": "Unscored has no colour: an Ink Soft word, a dashed Rule Strong scale with no fill, and a dash where a plate number would be. Never a zero, never a grey bar.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Archivo for anything that names, counts or controls; Source Serif 4 for anything that is read as a sentence. The admin is the exception that proves it: it is all controls, so it is all Archivo.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every numeral that can line up with another (plate numbers, Scores, ratings, counts, dates in meta) uses tabular figures.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Never Shrink Rule",
        "body": "Narrow screens drop columns and decoration, never the reading size: body stays at 1.0625rem; only display-scale numerals and titles step down.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Only The Works Hang Rule",
        "body": "Shadows are for covers. Placeholder covers, which are not works, drop the shadow and take a dashed outline.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** take every colour from the tokens in `app/globals.css`, and give each new role a light and a dark value.",
      "**Do** print the number next to any Score colour, and print the state word next to any status colour.",
      "**Do** use Archivo with its width axis for names, numerals and controls, and Source Serif 4 for sentences.",
      "**Do** separate plates, rows and sections with rules (1px hairline, 2px Ink, 3px double for a sum) rather than boxes.",
      "**Do** show absence with a dashed Rule Strong outline and an honest word: Unscored, no cover, no results.",
      "**Do** keep reading text at 1.0625rem on every screen width; drop columns instead.",
      "**Do** keep motion to the 160ms ease-out state fades, the cover lift, and the pull animation, all off under reduced motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add a hue outside the wall's blue family, the Score scale and the admin states.",
      "**Don't** fill a tile or card with a Score colour; the colour lives in the numeral and the meter fill.",
      "**Don't** show an Unscored Game as 0 or with a grey bar.",
      "**Don't** put shadows on anything but covers, and don't nest bordered containers inside one another.",
      "**Don't** shrink body text on narrow screens.",
      "**Don't** substitute a stock or generated image for a missing cover."
    ]
  }
}